ments we develop are setting standards in cardiac care.","source_heading":"DESCRIPTION","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Under the supervision of the on-duty charge nurse, the hospital telemetry technician carries out dysrhythmia monitoring responsibilities. Monitors, identifies, and reports to RN cardiac rhythms, arrhythmias, and any changes in baseline rhythm. Communicates with physicians and nurses any changes in rate, rhythm, measurements. Acts as resource to staff. Achieves trust in professional relationship with nursing staff and physicians.","source_heading":"DESCRIPTION","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"qualification","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Successful completion of a telemetry technician course/and or ECG training course.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null}],"pay":{"salary_min":32.52,"salary_max":null,"salary_period":"hour","annual_min":67641.6,"annual_max":67641.6,"annual_comparison":67641.6,"status":"usable","source":"scalar:hiring_pay_scale","source_heading":"hiring pay scale","source_text":"$32.52 / Hour","is_hourly_fte":true,"hours_per_unit":null},"published_at":"2026-11-27T17:19:46.598419+00:00"}
